WEBVTT

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.575
GAUNA: PROJECTED CORE

00:00:39.248 --> 00:00:40.123
There's too many of them.

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:49.675
HIGH LEVELS OF HEIGUS PARTICLES DETECTED

00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:51.051
Damn it!

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:10.153
MARK 17 GARDE LUNAR WHITE MODEL
TSUGUMORI VIRTUAL GARDE TRAINING SYSTEM

00:01:10.279 --> 00:01:11.530
VIRTUAL TRAINING COMPLETE

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:13.574
RANKING 1ST
NAGATE TANIKAZE 999999

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:21.290
Good, Tanikaze.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.874
Oh, thank you.

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:27.421
Listen up! With the automatic functions
of the Mark 18,

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:30.716
there's nothing he can do that
you can't do with the right training!

00:01:32.426 --> 00:01:34.636
So I want you to go out there
and give it everything you've got!

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.804
Yes, sir!

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.223
Tanikaze, why don't you
give them a few words?

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:43.520
What? Oh, um...
Everyone, do your best.

00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:45.731
Yes, sir.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:52.571
<i>Go forth and conquer!
<i>Let there be light!</i></i>

00:01:56.575 --> 00:02:01.872
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:08.629
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:12.799
KNIGHTS OF SIDONIA

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:22.726
<i>Our only haven is this fortress</i>

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.812
<i>Wandering among the stars</i>

00:02:25.896 --> 00:02:29.066
<i>Where we tremble with impatience</i>

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.485
<i>Between life and death</i>

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:37.240
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:42.079
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:50.212
<i>Those of us who have been led
<i>To gather here</i></i>

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:56.927
<i>Carry within ourselves the will to fight</i>

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.555
<i>Our lives shine their brightest</i>

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:03.058
<i>In the defense of love</i>

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.020
<i>We boldly enter the fray</i>

00:03:07.104 --> 00:03:11.525
<i>The Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:21.451
CONFLICT

00:03:26.581 --> 00:03:27.749
Master Norio!

00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:31.420
-Mozuku, go back.
-You mustn't, Master Norio!

00:03:31.503 --> 00:03:32.337
WARNING, WILL SHOOT TO KILL

00:03:32.421 --> 00:03:35.841
The Kunato Family will be finished
if they find out you opened that door.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.511
I'm finished either way...

00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:42.305
Just go.

00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:47.144
Very well.

00:03:48.395 --> 00:03:50.772
But I am not going anywhere.

00:03:51.523 --> 00:03:53.442
I am your shadow.

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:56.570
I will follow you to the end.

00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:17.632
What is this place?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.968
It's Ochiai's laboratory.

00:04:20.635 --> 00:04:23.764
I have heard it was sealed off
because research that could

00:04:24.014 --> 00:04:26.433
potentially destroy Sidonia
was being conducted here.

00:04:36.818 --> 00:04:38.987
What is this?

00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:45.035
Cacti?

00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:47.662
But there aren't any needles growing.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.505
Master Norio, run!

00:04:56.671 --> 00:04:57.714
What is it?!

00:04:59.216 --> 00:05:00.759
Mozuku! Are you okay?!

00:05:10.477 --> 00:05:11.394
Mozuku.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:43.385
It seems you're adjusting to
your new body well, Master Ochiai.

00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.973
Be careful not to address me
with that name.

00:05:48.974 --> 00:05:50.100
Mozuku.

00:05:50.392 --> 00:05:53.186
That's right. Kunato...

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:55.438
I mean...

00:05:57.315 --> 00:05:58.483
Master Norio.

00:06:02.153 --> 00:06:03.530
CLASSIFIED:
ACCESS DENIED PERMISSION DENIED

00:06:03.613 --> 00:06:05.031
Good.

00:06:08.952 --> 00:06:09.953
Well, well.

00:06:10.912 --> 00:06:14.666
This generation
has a pilot prodigy as well?

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:28.972
I see.

00:06:29.806 --> 00:06:33.643
So this is Saito's clone.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.363
Oh, no. I fell asleep.

00:06:47.115 --> 00:06:47.949
Yes.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:48.867
LIVE

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.243
<i>I'm from Kunato Development.</i>

00:06:50.368 --> 00:06:53.413
<i>I've come to view the ena sample.</i>

00:06:53.872 --> 00:06:54.706
What?

00:06:55.165 --> 00:06:57.667
I don't remember a request like that.

00:06:59.628 --> 00:07:00.503
VISIT: NORIO KUNATO
VISIT REQUEST: GRANTED

00:07:00.629 --> 00:07:02.672
Oh, it's true.
He's been granted access.

00:07:03.298 --> 00:07:05.800
Are you the pilot, Mr. Kunato?

00:07:06.635 --> 00:07:07.552
<i>Yes,</i>

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.054
<i>that's right.</i>

00:07:09.846 --> 00:07:10.680
MOZUKU KUNATO

00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:11.598
NORIO KUNATO

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:13.558
-Thank you for having us.
-I see.

00:07:13.642 --> 00:07:16.019
You decided to take the reins
of Kunato Development.

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.229
My father suddenly passed away.

00:07:18.939 --> 00:07:21.441
Oh, really?
I'm so sorry for your loss.

00:07:25.695 --> 00:07:29.157
We may have lost the garde manufacturing
contract to Toa Heavy Industries,

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.952
but we've been given the important
privilege of developing new research.

00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:33.995
As I did when I was a pilot,

00:07:34.204 --> 00:07:36.081
I plan on giving it my all.

00:07:36.831 --> 00:07:39.417
You seem very responsible
despite your young age.

00:07:39.793 --> 00:07:40.877
This way.

00:07:45.632 --> 00:07:47.092
Amazing.

00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:49.970
I couldn't ask for better.

00:07:50.971 --> 00:07:54.099
Ask for better...?

00:07:54.349 --> 00:07:56.434
Oh, nothing.

00:07:57.102 --> 00:08:00.313
The organs and brain have
been brilliantly reproduced.

00:08:00.605 --> 00:08:03.984
Functionally speaking, they are nearly
the same as a human being's.

00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:07.737
As it is,
gauna do not need to eat or breathe.

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.782
Their bodies are superior to humans.

00:08:11.866 --> 00:08:14.828
So why go through the trouble of

00:08:14.953 --> 00:08:18.456
reproducing the inferior
human biological functions?

00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:22.752
Every time I see a gauna,
I always think one thing.

00:08:23.253 --> 00:08:27.257
Humans must change the way
they are as living beings.

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:30.468
The way they are as living beings?

00:08:30.719 --> 00:08:31.845
For example,

00:08:32.303 --> 00:08:36.433
creating a single immortal life form.

00:08:39.144 --> 00:08:42.188
I used to have discussions like that.

00:08:42.772 --> 00:08:46.026
But I believe if individuals pursued
biological enhancements

00:08:46.109 --> 00:08:51.031
and achieved immortality,
we would no longer function as a tribe.

00:08:57.412 --> 00:09:02.917
I see. So the general population
doesn't know about the Immortal Council.

00:09:03.293 --> 00:09:04.294
What?

00:09:04.794 --> 00:09:08.006
Tribalism is an outdated concept.

00:09:08.256 --> 00:09:11.926
Thinking of such primitive creatures
spreading across the universe

00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:15.221
and consuming everything in their path...

00:09:15.722 --> 00:09:16.931
It makes me sick.

00:09:17.348 --> 00:09:19.517
What are you saying?

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:22.687
You're all pathetic creatures

00:09:22.937 --> 00:09:24.856
reeking of fetid garbage,

00:09:24.981 --> 00:09:28.777
dribbling excrement everywhere you go.

00:09:30.278 --> 00:09:32.572
What's wrong with you?

00:09:32.781 --> 00:09:34.282
I'm going to call someone.

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:42.874
Unfortunately,

00:09:43.124 --> 00:09:48.421
you will probably never move this body
under your own will ever again.

00:09:49.214 --> 00:09:51.800
This is my own creation,
the Sidonia Blood Nematode.

00:09:52.383 --> 00:09:54.385
One this size can completely transcribe

00:09:54.469 --> 00:09:56.721
the human brain
or artificial intelligence.

00:09:57.347 --> 00:10:00.308
The new personality will
take over the host's brain,

00:10:00.642 --> 00:10:02.644
and will be in control of the body.

00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:26.918
How was your triumphant
return to cadet school?

00:10:27.085 --> 00:10:30.755
I was really nervous.
I didn't know what to say.

00:10:31.047 --> 00:10:32.590
Everyone was looking at me.

00:10:32.799 --> 00:10:34.092
Of course they were.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.470
You're every pilot cadet's hero.

00:10:37.929 --> 00:10:40.849
They asked you about
the asteroid battle, didn't they?

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.226
Yeah...

00:10:49.691 --> 00:10:50.567
Tahiro!

00:10:51.609 --> 00:10:53.278
Where is Hoshijiro?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:58.283
Pilot Tanikaze,
Pilot Hoshijiro is deceased.

00:10:58.908 --> 00:11:00.827
What was kept here was
just an ena sample.

00:11:05.832 --> 00:11:06.791
What's wrong?

00:11:07.417 --> 00:11:09.878
It's nothing.

00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:12.005
Okay...

00:11:16.217 --> 00:11:17.343
It's hot.

00:11:18.469 --> 00:11:19.512
Thank you for the meal.

00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:21.222
What? That's all you're eating?

00:11:21.389 --> 00:11:22.557
That's unusual.

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:24.058
You're not having seconds?

00:11:24.392 --> 00:11:26.603
No. That's enough for today.

00:11:27.478 --> 00:11:28.605
It was very good.

00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:37.071
Hoshijiro!

00:11:44.621 --> 00:11:46.539
Hoshijiro?

00:12:03.598 --> 00:12:09.479
SITES OF SIDONIA
WEST 4 GARDE HANGAR ACCESSWAY

00:12:16.903 --> 00:12:17.904
Tahiro!

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:21.741
I was just coming to see you!

00:12:21.824 --> 00:12:23.618
I wanted to talk again
about last time.

00:12:24.202 --> 00:12:25.745
About the ena sample?

00:12:26.412 --> 00:12:27.455
Kunato...

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.165
how do you know about that?

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:31.417
The Extraterrestrial Research Division

00:12:31.501 --> 00:12:33.586
transferred the sample
to Kunato Development.

00:12:34.629 --> 00:12:36.089
I can't tell you the details,

00:12:36.172 --> 00:12:38.466
but don't worry.
It's for the good of Sidonia.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.344
Wait! Stop!

00:12:41.511 --> 00:12:44.764
What do you mean?
Don't tell me you're cutting her up!

00:12:45.098 --> 00:12:46.432
Pilot Tanikaze,

00:12:46.557 --> 00:12:48.309
that thing is just an ena.

00:12:48.643 --> 00:12:52.063
It seems you had some sort of
special feelings for Shizuka Hoshijiro,

00:12:52.146 --> 00:12:54.065
but you can't give them
any consideration here.

00:12:55.191 --> 00:12:58.027
Your battle against the Crimson
Hawk Moth was quite impressive.

00:12:58.111 --> 00:12:59.237
You have my support!

00:13:07.203 --> 00:13:09.664
Do you think this is enough for his lunch?

00:13:09.914 --> 00:13:13.668
Probably. Nagate seems to
have lost his appetite lately.

00:13:13.918 --> 00:13:16.713
Do you think it's about that ena sample?

00:13:17.505 --> 00:13:21.050
The Extraterrestrial Research Division
was calling him in all the time,

00:13:21.134 --> 00:13:22.635
but not anymore.

00:13:23.261 --> 00:13:26.889
I asked Nagate about it,
but he won't tell me anything.

00:13:27.265 --> 00:13:28.975
Just give him some space.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.227
He's still eating.

00:13:33.271 --> 00:13:34.480
You're right.

00:13:35.231 --> 00:13:36.899
Have fun tomorrow.

00:13:37.775 --> 00:13:39.694
Thank you, Ms. Hiyama!

00:13:41.529 --> 00:13:43.364
What?!

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:44.657
I'm sorry.

00:13:44.866 --> 00:13:46.784
I'll be back as soon as I can.

00:13:47.368 --> 00:13:49.370
I even made you lunch!

00:13:50.705 --> 00:13:52.165
You can't do it over the phone?

00:13:52.331 --> 00:13:53.166
No.

00:13:53.249 --> 00:13:56.669
Yuhata said she wanted to
talk to me about the ena sample.

00:13:58.629 --> 00:14:00.965
Fine. I'll just go by myself.

00:14:01.132 --> 00:14:02.383
Izana!

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:08.848
Yuhata.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.894
I'm sorry for making you
meet on such short notice.

00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:14.854
Actually, the captain gave an order

00:14:15.146 --> 00:14:16.939
concerning the ena sample.

00:14:17.231 --> 00:14:18.191
What was it?

00:14:18.566 --> 00:14:20.651
Don't get involved with the ena anymore.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:25.740
The captain seemed
very worried for you, Tanikaze.

00:14:26.908 --> 00:14:30.286
I think that means
she's counting on you as a pilot.

00:14:31.162 --> 00:14:33.831
Okay, I understand.

00:14:34.207 --> 00:14:37.377
I won't look for that ena anymore.

00:14:38.211 --> 00:14:40.755
I'll forget the whole thing,
Sub-commander Midorikawa!

00:14:41.005 --> 00:14:44.217
Good. You do that, Pilot Tanikaze.

00:14:45.009 --> 00:14:45.885
You're excused.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:50.098
Is something the matter?

00:14:50.348 --> 00:14:52.100
Oh, well...

00:15:04.821 --> 00:15:07.365
I've got a long way to go.

00:15:12.578 --> 00:15:14.455
This isn't fun at all.

00:15:22.255 --> 00:15:23.214
Hey!

00:15:23.798 --> 00:15:24.632
Izana!

00:15:24.882 --> 00:15:26.342
Nagate!

00:15:26.717 --> 00:15:28.177
What is that?

00:15:28.261 --> 00:15:30.888
It's an evacuation jet pack
for upper level crew members.

00:15:31.013 --> 00:15:33.141
Yuhata let me use it.

00:15:33.433 --> 00:15:34.642
She did?

00:15:35.476 --> 00:15:37.019
Oh, thank God!

00:15:37.437 --> 00:15:39.188
There's still rice balls left!

00:15:42.358 --> 00:15:45.361
Like I could eat them all by myself!

00:16:00.793 --> 00:16:03.588
Why do I have to go out of my way

00:16:03.671 --> 00:16:05.715
to help those two?

00:16:12.472 --> 00:16:14.557
We used up most of the man-made kabi

00:16:14.724 --> 00:16:19.479
we created from the hybrid
in the asteroid battle.

00:16:19.896 --> 00:16:23.608
And then suddenly Kunato Development
manages to manufacture a ton in no time?

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.278
We're practically swimming in
gauna core-piercing rounds now.

00:16:27.904 --> 00:16:30.031
What kind of magic did they use?

00:16:30.656 --> 00:16:33.743
They said they found
a new manufacturing method.

00:16:34.035 --> 00:16:35.745
And what new method is that?

00:16:36.204 --> 00:16:38.247
How in the world?!

00:16:38.539 --> 00:16:40.291
That's what anybody would think.

00:16:48.299 --> 00:16:49.217
Where's the gauna?!

00:16:49.509 --> 00:16:52.720
Gauna 549 has already crossed
the level 2 security border.

00:16:52.929 --> 00:16:54.764
It's currently 360,000 kilometers away!

00:16:55.056 --> 00:16:56.474
The analysis is coming in!

00:16:58.017 --> 00:17:00.353
-It's big. Is it a gauna pod?
-No.

00:17:00.436 --> 00:17:01.812
We're estimating
there's only a single core.

00:17:01.896 --> 00:17:02.730
CORE LOCATION

00:17:02.939 --> 00:17:03.773
A single core?

00:17:03.856 --> 00:17:07.735
Its mass is at least twice
the size of the gauna pod we encountered.

00:17:08.736 --> 00:17:13.157
We will proceed to destroy Gauna 549!
Garde squad, prepare for dispatch!

00:17:13.366 --> 00:17:14.992
Wait! We need a little more time.

00:17:15.201 --> 00:17:17.787
I haven't briefed the pilots yet.

00:17:18.412 --> 00:17:20.289
While they look the same,

00:17:20.623 --> 00:17:23.292
this is different from
the Tsugumori you've been piloting.

00:17:24.085 --> 00:17:24.919
Damn it.

00:17:25.461 --> 00:17:28.339
I wanted to give it a test flight
before we sent you out.

00:17:32.051 --> 00:17:34.887
Don't push it too hard.

00:17:35.304 --> 00:17:37.974
You'll have to answer to me
if you break my upgraded Tsugumori.

00:17:39.183 --> 00:17:40.268
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:42.103 --> 00:17:43.479
There's only one target,

00:17:43.688 --> 00:17:46.857
and only one single core.
But it is massive.

00:17:46.983 --> 00:17:48.192
Don't let your guard down.

00:17:48.359 --> 00:17:51.153
<i>I'm sorry I'm late.
<i>Tanikaze, ready to launch!</i></i>

00:18:15.052 --> 00:18:17.680
Tanikaze is traveling
fast for being a single unit.

00:18:18.097 --> 00:18:20.099
We're in a four unit clasp formation
and he's going to catch up to us.

00:18:21.434 --> 00:18:23.352
Whoa, what the hell is that output?

00:18:23.686 --> 00:18:25.646
Tanikaze, taking point.

00:18:30.818 --> 00:18:33.821
All units have entered effective
range for piercing rounds!

00:18:34.113 --> 00:18:35.406
The enemy is massive.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.575
Follow the plan and keep your distance.

00:18:38.242 --> 00:18:41.370
Tanikaze will proceed to fire
from the effective range limit.

00:18:41.829 --> 00:18:44.790
All other units will fall into
the wedge formation and support.

00:18:45.124 --> 00:18:45.958
Copy that!

00:18:46.167 --> 00:18:47.001
<i>Affirmative!</i>

00:18:47.251 --> 00:18:49.587
Tanikaze, firing!

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:51.130
PROJECTED CORE LOCATION

00:19:02.016 --> 00:19:02.850
That's strange.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.103
The gauna core's unharmed!

00:19:06.354 --> 00:19:09.523
The core-piercing rounds are
being stopped at the gauna's surface!

00:19:09.732 --> 00:19:10.566
What?!

00:19:10.983 --> 00:19:13.235
-How's that possible?
-It must be a mistake.

00:19:13.402 --> 00:19:14.779
No...

00:19:15.696 --> 00:19:17.490
Structural analysis is complete!

00:19:18.949 --> 00:19:19.825
What's this?

00:19:20.076 --> 00:19:23.162
Conventional ena cells
and core shell ena cells are

00:19:23.412 --> 00:19:24.747
layered on top of each other.

00:19:27.208 --> 00:19:28.626
I can't believe
they developed countermeasures

00:19:28.709 --> 00:19:30.252
for our core-piercing rounds this quickly.

00:19:30.419 --> 00:19:33.631
Damn it! How are we supposed
to destroy the core?

00:19:34.131 --> 00:19:37.677
I think we should have all units
fire at the same location!

00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:41.097
<i>If we destroy the ena faster
<i>than it can regenerate,</i></i>

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.516
<i>we should be able to
<i>penetrate the core eventually.</i></i>

00:19:45.559 --> 00:19:47.520
That seems like our only option.

00:19:48.187 --> 00:19:50.940
Operator, calculate the entry point
with shortest distance

00:19:51.065 --> 00:19:54.819
from the gauna surface to the core
and send it out to the units!

00:19:55.236 --> 00:19:56.070
Affirmative!

00:19:56.404 --> 00:19:57.947
SHORTEST ENTRY POINT
CORE LOCATION

00:19:58.531 --> 00:20:01.117
All units,
focus your attacks on this location!

00:20:01.283 --> 00:20:02.118
<i>Affirmative!</i>

00:20:05.705 --> 00:20:08.207
<i>All units, watch your firing
<i>angle to the impact point.</i></i>

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.793
<i>Attack in waves and maintain
<i>double echelon formation.</i></i>

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.967
Several impacts to the target point!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.927
We've broken through the core shell ena!

00:20:20.094 --> 00:20:22.388
<i>The ena is regenerating
<i>faster than I thought.</i></i>

00:20:22.638 --> 00:20:25.474
<i>We need to finish it off soon
<i>or we'll run out of ammunition.</i></i>

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:29.395
Sixty percent until gauna core impact!

00:20:29.562 --> 00:20:30.563
Just a little more...

00:20:36.277 --> 00:20:39.029
Sudden Heigus particle
increase in Gauna 549!

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:40.531
All units, scatter!

00:20:49.457 --> 00:20:53.502
We can't concentrate on
aiming while dodging its attack.

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:56.797
<i>The damaged ena is regenerating!</i>

00:20:57.131 --> 00:20:57.965
What?!

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.676
<i>Attack squad core-penetration round
<i>reserves at 20 percent!</i></i>

00:21:02.094 --> 00:21:02.928
Tanikaze!

00:21:03.053 --> 00:21:05.306
Is he planning on taking down
the enemy's ena cannons on his own?

00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:11.437
Tanikaze!

00:21:13.898 --> 00:21:15.566
Ena, still regenerating!

00:21:15.858 --> 00:21:18.652
We've dropped down to 20 percent
until gauna core impact!

00:21:19.278 --> 00:21:21.530
All units on standby, prepare for attack!

00:21:21.906 --> 00:21:24.116
All units,
equip gauna core-piercing rounds!

00:21:25.993 --> 00:21:26.994
What's this?

00:21:27.453 --> 00:21:30.664
A new gauna? It appeared
from the final defensive line?!

00:21:30.831 --> 00:21:32.333
The new gauna has accelerated!

00:21:32.416 --> 00:21:33.834
It's continuing to accelerate.

00:21:33.918 --> 00:21:36.337
It's traveling several times faster than
a garde's conventional operation speed!

00:21:36.587 --> 00:21:39.882
The second gauna's target trajectory
is heading towards Tanikaze and Ren!

00:21:40.216 --> 00:21:44.678
<i>Tanikaze, Ren, get away from there!
<i>Another gauna is headed right for you!</i></i>

00:21:44.887 --> 00:21:47.598
We've got other things
we're dealing with...

00:21:47.973 --> 00:21:51.018
High levels of Heigus particles
detected from the new gauna!

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:52.394
What?!

00:22:08.994 --> 00:22:10.371
Very nice shot.

00:22:10.955 --> 00:22:11.997
Good girl.

00:22:13.082 --> 00:22:14.792
<i>Thank you, Father.</i>

00:22:19.672 --> 00:22:21.674
What is that?

00:22:22.424 --> 00:22:23.884
What is it?

00:22:30.891 --> 00:22:32.935
Hello, everybody.

00:22:33.394 --> 00:22:36.230
My name is Tsumugi Shiraui.
It's nice to meet you.

00:22:36.855 --> 00:22:38.816
I look forward to getting to know you all.

00:22:40.818 --> 00:22:42.444
TO BE CONTINUED

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:50.828
<i>Oh, if this world must decay</i>

00:22:50.911 --> 00:22:54.582
<i>And I'm destined to give my life away</i>

00:22:54.665 --> 00:22:59.753
<i>What should I be living for?</i>

00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:05.676
<i>If I had never met you</i>

00:23:05.759 --> 00:23:09.346
<i>I would never have known</i>

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:15.352
<i>This pain that tears at my heart</i>

00:23:15.436 --> 00:23:17.771
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-Echoing there</i></i>

00:23:17.855 --> 00:23:19.857
<i>-Fortune
<i>-In the furthest reaches of the cosmos</i></i>

00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:22.860
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Is this clumsy requiem</i></i>

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.237
<i>-To be the sport of fortune
<i>-And yet</i></i>

00:23:25.321 --> 00:23:27.156
<i>-Fortune
<i>-I'm still searching</i></i>

00:23:27.239 --> 00:23:30.576
<i>-Fortune
<i>-Within this uncertain reality</i></i>

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.661
<i>For you</i>

00:23:32.745 --> 00:23:36.373
<i>The joy of our finding each other</i>

00:23:36.457 --> 00:23:40.085
<i>The vanished warmth</i>

00:23:40.169 --> 00:23:43.797
<i>You should know that I remember it all</i>

00:23:43.881 --> 00:23:47.551
<i>Because I loved you</i>

00:23:47.635 --> 00:23:51.221
<i>The emotions that arise</i>

00:23:51.305 --> 00:23:54.850
<i>The scars left in my heart</i>

00:23:54.933 --> 00:23:59.271
<i>You should know that I'll carry them all</i>

00:23:59.355 --> 00:24:05.944
<i>As I walk this path</i>
